<article class="env-definition" id="07IG">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/07IG">Definition <span data-tag="07IG">60.9.1</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/07MF" data-tag="07MF">60.7.5</a>. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
The (small) <em>crystalline site</em> of $X$ over $(S, \mathcal{I}, \gamma )$, denoted $\text{Cris}(X/S, \mathcal{I}, \gamma )$ or simply $\text{Cris}(X/S)$ is the full subcategory of $\text{CRIS}(X/S)$ consisting of those $(U, T, \delta )$ in $\text{CRIS}(X/S)$ such that $U \to X$ is an open immersion. It comes endowed with the Zariski topology. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
The topos of sheaves on $\text{Cris}(X/S)$ is denoted $(X/S)_{\text{cris}}$ or sometimes $(X/S, \mathcal{I}, \gamma )_{\text{cris}}$<a class="footnotemark" href="#a0001272608" id="a0001272608-mark"><sup>1</sup></a>. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>